# Line-ending policy.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: a byte-compared artifact with no `eol=lf` has an
# UNARMED freshness gate on Windows. Git stores LF, autocrlf checks out CRLF,
# and the committed file is then not byte-identical to a fresh emission — so an
# `emit && git diff --exit-code` check reports the whole file as changed, and a
# comparison that NORMALIZES line endings first cannot see the difference it
# normalizes. Found by Vulkane on a generated manifest, 2026-08-20.
#
# ADDING A BYTE-COMPARED OR HASH-VERIFIED ARTIFACT? Pin it here, or its gate is
# decorative on half the machines that run it.

# Licence files are hash-verified against canonical upstream text. Without this
# pin, autocrlf re-diverges them on the next Windows checkout and the hash check
# fails for a reason nobody guesses.
LICENSE-*       text eol=lf
LICENSE         text eol=lf

# Vendored conformance corpus — byte-matched against KISS's published artifact.
# Not currently exposed (our byte-match parses JSON first, so line endings never
# reach the token comparison) but pinned so a future byte-level compare is armed.
*.json          text eol=lf
